42sh, built from github.com/Polturgust/my-shell, running on a small
Linux in your browser. ls, cat, grep... come from BusyBox.

Tab completes   Up/Down history   Ctrl+R search   Ctrl+Z suspend

Try:  ls -la | grep txt            cat fruits.txt | sort -r > s.txt
      set name = you               echo "hello $name" `pwd`
      cd pro  (press Tab)          ./hello.sh && echo ok || echo no
      sleep 20 &                   jobs ; fg  (then Ctrl+C)
      alias ll ls -l               history ; !!

